      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the Lower Chehalis word “ts‑a‑lis,” meaning “place of sand.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westport%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A U.S. Army fort was built there in 1860, long before Westport was founded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westport%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Westport’s Lifesaving Station, established in 1871, became a Coast Guard station in 1917 and still marks the harbor entrance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
